s have stream implementations that satisfy the commuting law;\n1061:Cranelift's real advantages are build simplicity and compile speed, which matter for a REPL and\n1149:the web are both conforming implementations, because no program can observe which one it got.\n1224:feature in the wrong position. Measured against a jq implementation:\n1574:Prototype 1 implemented no value-to-effect shifter at all, taking\n1599:### Masking now has an implementation to argue with\n1653:benchmark: every candidate answer was already implied by something the language had committed to,\n1706:and the checker implements exactly one member of it: `expect` special-cases `input` and falls\n1717:glossary has no term for it because the language has not decided. Sugar that quietly implements\n1822:used at two disagreeing types, simplified to \"used at all, twice.\" Python's generators are the\n1867:Rust-side reimplementation instead. `None` (the real command-line case) connects the live stdin.\n1879:still runs, verified rather than replaced by a Rust-side reimplementation feeding a pre-split\n2019:is not an operand of anything, so `+ y` is simply left over and rejected as trailing garbage\n2116:  question answered from the other side: native's vector implementation (and other targets)\n2149:kantord/toylang#63) for serialization and friends, not implemented by this decision.\n2203:implementation disclosed a cross-function hole (a function reading a source, called from a\n2207:rejected as an invisible effect on every signature, the implicit shape this design keeps\n2266:implemented yet, and `3.14` in the values list above is still only notation.\n2328:user-written type declaration the language has, and it is prioritized ahead of implementing\n2369:minimal implementation: variant arms chained with `//`, `.` rebinding to the payload inside\n","metadata":{"output":"41:inserted implicitly:\n92:a \"project\" trait. (I guess we could have a convention that traits are methods with __ as prefix and suff