{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788379907055,"sessionID":"ses_f9c41a182ffeXV0U7B2A3hfjyw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_4a15876d73fa40b7a6aaa51c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"x:foo\\|receiver\\|colon-only\\|:foo\\|method call\\|method-call\" draft.md | head -30"},"output":"673:power. Sketch offered and explicitly flagged as a bad first attempt at syntax: `b:foo{mul(\"a\")}b`\n674:in place of `ba*b`, and `b:foo:b` in place of `b.*b`.\n691:iterable receivers. What would need stating, and is not yet, is the law the two implementations\n886:level**: one semantics stated as a trait, with a different implementation when the receiver is a\n","metadata":{"output":"673:power. Sketch offered and explicitly flagged as a bad first attempt at syntax: `b:foo{mul(\"a\")}b`\n674:in place of `ba*b`, and `b:foo:b` in place of `b.*b`.\n691:iterable receivers. What would need stating, and is not yet, is the law the two implementations\n886:level**: one semantics stated as a trait, with a different implementation when the receiver is a\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"x:foo\\|receiver\\|colon-only\\|:foo\\|method call\\|method-call\" draft.md | head -30","time":{"start":1788379907051,"end":1788379907052}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me look at the section about method-call colon form in draft.md and any design decisions about the trait mechanism. Let me search for \"colon\" and \"receiver\".","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_063bfc3c9001h8IwRqNb3Vs7g4","sessionID":"ses_f9c41a182ffeXV0U7B2A3hfjyw","messageID":"msg_063bfb3bb0018cOo6V8Zr4SRsW"}}
