{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788379908492,"sessionID":"ses_f9c41a182ffeXV0U7B2A3hfjyw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_e198f28992c3446c9fffa5d7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"x:foo\\|:foo\\|colon\\|receiver\" plans/board-archive.yaml | head -30"},"output":"1225:  title: 'Grill method-like call syntax -- round 1 ratified UFCS-style desugaring (x.foo(y) -> foo(x,y)); the operator spelling (dot vs an alternative like `:`) and whether the receiver form curries are still open, needs a round 2 (gh:119) -- ruled: colon operator (`x:foo(y)`); \"curried\" redefined away from this round''s framing -- maintainer: \"five_plus(1, 2) should not be correct, either five_plus(1) is correct (but still becomes curried) or five_plus [1, 2] is correct; also function will still always only have one parameter; a true curried function would be a function that returns another function\" -- spins off partial-application-system-design (gh:119)'\n1358:  title: 'Grill the concrete trait/impl syntax and dispatch mechanism (overloading-and-utf8-lines round ruling spinoff), informed by trait-interface-research -- ruled: (1) declaration-syntax: A, Rust-shaped trait{}/impl X for Type{}; (2) builtin-operator-impl-representation: tentative hybrid, prelude impls when practical otherwise checker-generated, maintainer declined to fully commit (\"we would need to see how it works out in practice\"); (3) trait-method-receiver-spelling: A, colon-only x:foo(y), no plain-call fallback. Spins off trait-interface-build.'\n","metadata":{"output":"1225:  title: 'Grill method-like call syntax -- round 1 ratified UFCS-style desugaring (x.foo(y) -> foo(x,y)); the operator spelling (dot vs an alternative like `:`) and whether the receiver form curries are still open, needs a round 2 (gh:119) -- ruled: colon operator (`x:foo(y)`); \"curried\" redefined away from this round''s framing -- maintainer: \"five_plus(1, 2) should not be correct, either five_plus(1) is correct (but still becomes curried) or five_plus [1, 2] is correct; also function will still always only have one parameter; a true curried function would be a function that returns another function\" -- spins off partial-application-system-design (gh:119)'\n1358:  title: 'Grill the concrete trait/impl syntax and dispatch mechanism (overloading-and-utf8-lines round ruling spinoff), informed by trait-interface-research -- ruled: (1) declaration-syntax: A, Rust-shaped trait{}/impl X for Type{}; (2) builtin-operator-impl-representation: tentative hybrid, prelude impls when practical otherwise checker-generated, maintainer declined to fully commit (\"we would need to see how it works out in practice\"); (3) trait-method-receiver-spelling: A, colon-only x:foo(y), no plain-call fallback. Spins off trait-interface-build.'\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"x:foo\\|:foo\\|colon\\|receiver\" plans/board-archive.yaml | head -30","time":{"start":1788379908487,"end":1788379908489}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me check the board-archive.yaml for the `overloading-and-traits-design` ruling and any details on the colon call form (`x:foo(y)`).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_063bfc97a001RzESIZp0qxKNXD","sessionID":"ses_f9c41a182ffeXV0U7B2A3hfjyw","messageID":"msg_063bfc3ff001nmtHoBOsaTauKX"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788379908492,"sessionID":"ses_f9c41a182ffeXV0U7B2A3hfjyw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_13e975a5b5f14e8393dba5ad","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"gh:119\\|gh:174\\|gh:152\" plans/board-archive.yaml plans/board.yaml draft.md | head -20"},"output":"plans/board-archive.yaml:1075:  title: \"Grill destructuring params and pipeline-first bodies -- ruled: direction only, implicit . + matching syntax, spelling deferred (gh:152)\"\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1224:  issue: gh:119\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1225:  title: 'Grill method-like call syntax -- round 1 ratified UFCS-style desugaring (x.foo(y) -> foo(x,y)); the operator spelling (dot vs an alternative like `:`) and whether the receiver form curries are still open, needs a round 2 (gh:119) -- ruled: colon operator (`x:foo(y)`); \"curried\" redefined away from this round''s framing -- maintainer: \"five_plus(1, 2) should not be correct, either five_plus(1) is correct (but still becomes curried) or five_plus [1, 2] is correct; also function will still always only have one parameter; a true curried function would be a function that returns another function\" -- spins off partial-application-system-design (gh:119)'\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1350:  issue: gh:152\nplans/board.yaml:14:  issue: gh:152\nplans/board.yaml:15:  title: 'Grill the concrete spelling for implicit-. params via matching syntax -- round 1 couldn''t pick without more context; round 2 presents the maintainer''s own hoist-into-signature sketch (fn render = Msg(Ping -> ... or ...)) as a concrete candidate (gh:152). Round 2 answer: no pick yet; round 3 stress-tested each of the three candidates (A/B/C) against the real parser and re-asked. Round 3 answer: still no pick, needs signature-matching-deeper-research first; round 4 presented that research (all six type shapes) with full code probes per option. Round 4 answer: still no pick, and it is process feedback, not a content signal -- option cards were too long (\"at least 8 times shorter\"), code belongs once in the thesis not repeated per option, and rounds should frame how each option interacts with future plans rather than asking for an early commit. grill-via-annotations/SKILL.md''s option-card rule updated to match (2026-09-02). Round 5 must re-ask the same A/B/C content (A and B still fail identically pre-shape, C still the only candidate that parses all six shapes) in the new short-card, future-framed shape -- no new research needed.'\nplans/board.yaml:238:  issue: gh:119\nplans/board.yaml:246:  issue: gh:119\nplans/board.yaml:247:  title: 'Grill array-like vs struct-like partial application for the colon method-call operator (gh:119 ruling spinoff), informed by closures-first-class-functions-research -- maintainer: \"either five_plus(1) is correct (but still becomes curried) or five_plus [1, 2] is correct; also function will still always only have one parameter; a true curried function would be a function that returns another function; we may want to implement this, or perhaps consider instead thinking about formalizing at least the beginning of a partial application system which could either apply a partial array-like or a partial struct-like\"'\n","metadata":{"output":"plans/board-archive.yaml:1075:  title: \"Grill destructuring params and pipeline-first bodies -- ruled: direction only, implicit . + matching syntax, spelling deferred (gh:152)\"\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1224:  issue: gh:119\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1225:  title: 'Grill method-like call syntax -- round 1 ratified UFCS-style desugaring (x.foo(y) -> foo(x,y)); the operator spelling (dot vs an alternative like `:`) and whether the receiver form curries are still open, needs a round 2 (gh:119) -- ruled: colon operator (`x:foo(y)`); \"curried\" redefined away from this round''s framing -- maintainer: \"five_plus(1, 2) should not be correct, either five_plus(1) is correct (but still becomes curried) or five_plus [1, 2] is correct; also function will still always only have one parameter; a true curried function would be a function that returns another function\" -- spins off partial-application-system-design (gh:119)'\nplans/board-archive.yaml:1350:  issue: gh:152\nplans/board.yaml:14:  issue: gh:152\nplans/board.yaml:15:  title: 'Grill the concrete spelling for implicit-. params via matching syntax -- round 1 couldn''t pick without more context; round 2 presents the maintainer''s own hoist-into-signature sketch (fn render = Msg(Ping -> ... or ...)) as a concrete candidate (gh:152). Round 2 answer: no pick yet; round 3 stress-tested each of the three candidates (A/B/C) against the real parser and re-asked. Round 3 answer: still no pick, needs signature-matching-deeper-research first; round 4 presented that research (all six type shapes) with full code probes per option. Round 4 answer: still no pick, and it is process feedback, not a content signal -- option cards were too long (\"at least 8 times shorter\"), code belongs once in the thesis not repeated per option, and rounds should frame how each option interacts with future plans rather than asking for an early commit. grill-via-annotations/SKILL.md''s option-card rule updated to match (2026-09-02). Round 5 must re-ask the same A/B/C content (A and B still fail identically pre-shape, C still the only candidate that parses all six shapes) in the new short-card, future-framed shape -- no new research needed.'\nplans/board.yaml:238:  issue: gh:119\nplans/board.yaml:246:  issue: gh:119\nplans/board.yaml:247:  title: 'Grill array-like vs struct-like partial application for the colon method-call operator (gh:119 ruling spinoff), informed by closures-first-class-functions-research -- maintainer: \"either five_plus(1) is correct (but still becomes curried) or five_plus [1, 2] is correct; also function will still always only have one parameter; a true curried function would be a function that returns another function; we may want to implement this, or perhaps consider instead thinking about formalizing at least the beginning of a partial application system which could either apply a partial array-like or a partial struct-like\"'\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -n \"gh:119\\|gh:174\\|gh:152\" plans/board-archive.yaml plans/board.yaml draft.md | head -20","time":{"start":1788379908490,"end":1788379908491}},"id":"prt_063bfc982001FQmBCoDzYaiaBP","sessionID":"ses_f9c41a182ffeXV0U7B2A3hfjyw","messageID":"msg_063bfc3ff001nmtHoBOsaTauKX"}}
